---
source: crates/wolf_mem/tests/mem_diagnostics.rs
expression: render_mem(src)
---
error[E1010]: `helper` builds in its caller's region and may leave a proc running that reads those bytes after it returns; here that is region `pass`, which is freed with its scope — while the proc may still be reading them
  --> mem:///main.lu:12:9
   |
 7 |     let _w = spawn proc child(s, 0)
   |              ---------------------- `child` is spawned here, and not every path out of the function joins it before it returns
...
11 |     region pass {
   |            ---- region `pass` is created here and freed with its scope — everything in it is freed wholesale
12 |         helper(n)
   |         ^^^^^^^^^ `helper` allocates into region `pass` at this call ([mem.region.create.3])
   |
   = note: a function that spawns a proc with bytes its caller owns must join that proc on every
     path before it returns — `p.join()`, an exit received from `p.monitor()`, or `p` handed
     to a function that does so; a kill is not a join, the proc may run on until it is joined
     (wolf-lang#683) — or the bytes must outlive the calling frame [conc.proc.arg]. Here the
     function may return with the proc still running, so the bytes it was handed must outlive
     this frame [mem.region.escape]. Join the proc in the callee on every path, or build the
     value where it outlives this frame — outside the region block; a literal or a scalar
     argument owns no region storage.
